#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100538 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d68c23-6a62-538d-adf1-3a20a474f107" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Midpoint Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "fd6cab66-924e-5fbf-8800-53b10e1e6623" :question/math-academy-id "e-3207" :question/problem "Find the coordinates $(h,k)$ of the center of the circle above given that the points $(2,-3)$ and $(10,5)$ lie on a diameter of the circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1183/Source/Images/eab58ac1804896bc3b18dcaac02635ff.png)" :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. Therefore, we can calculate it using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} (h,k) &= \\left(\\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2}, \\dfrac {y_1+y_2}{2}\\right) \\\\[2pt] &= \\left(\\dfrac{10+2}2,\\dfrac{5+(-3)}2\\right) \\\\[2pt] &= \\left(\\dfrac{12}2,\\dfrac{2}2\\right) \\\\[2pt] &= (6, 1). \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100539 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e9df1ae-8176-555b-987d-94773c27d435" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Distance Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "f091473d-0317-5c94-999f-4626dd93d021" :question/math-academy-id "e-3208" :question/problem "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-5,3)$ and $(-3,7)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overline{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Find the radius of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\sqrt{(x_{1} - x_{2})^{2} + (y_{1} - y_{2})^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-5 - (-3))^{2} + (3 - 7)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-2)^{2} + (-4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4 + 16} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{20} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr = \\dfrac{d}{2} = \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2} = \\sqrt{5}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100540 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52384502-66c5-5089-b38f-d46b94877430" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "4441ee7d-39ac-5aaf-ae23-aea9e9eb7ec7" :question/math-academy-id "e-3209" :question/problem "The segment $\\overline{CD}$ is the diameter of a circle where the points $C$ and $D$ have coordinates $(7a,6a)$ and $(a,-2a)$, respectively, with $a>0$. Find the coordinates of the center and the radius of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(h, k) &= (\\frac{x_{1} + x_{2}}{2}, \\frac{y_{1} + y_{2}}{2}) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{7a + a}{2}, (6a + (-2a))/(2)) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{8a}{2}, \\frac{4a}{2}) \\\\\n&= (4a, 2a)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(4a, 2a)$ and a point on the circle, such as $C(7a,6a)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr &= \\sqrt{(x_{1} - x_{2})^{2} + (y_{1} - y_{2})^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(4a - 7a)^{2} + (2a - 6a)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-3a)^{2} + (-4a)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9a^{2} + 16a^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25a^{2}} \\\\\n&= 5 \\mid a \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $a>0$, we have that\n\n$$\nr = 5\\vert a \\vert = 5a\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center of the circle is at $(4a, 2a)$ and the radius is $5a$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d68c23-6a62-538d-adf1-3a20a474f107" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Midpoint Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "543d558f-a63c-561f-ad1c-f9e517906d8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267168} {:answer/id #uuid "12350077-8d4c-5f7f-82e1-42f6e919d9a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267169} {:answer/id #uuid "8119782f-ed86-502b-bdaf-198b052ef42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267170} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b53343-0ade-555d-953d-b73a28d7722f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267171} {:answer/id #uuid "48c0065c-b69b-5a78-b941-99dc6d94cabb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8119782f-ed86-502b-bdaf-198b052ef42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267170} :answer-field/id #uuid "f78020d2-e0eb-5e6f-8813-9b5c36ad1a7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267167}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c2202cc-507a-53bf-ac22-4c5f6d40acb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-115346" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956659/assets/84a9754d9291ba38d6cd257056d20896ce2ff89b8ee98210c8789fc9d633ae5f.png)\n\nFind the coordinates $(h,k)$ of the center of the circle above given that the points $(-1,4)$ and $(-7,-4)$ lie on a diameter of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. Therefore, we can calculate it using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-1-7}{2},\\frac{4-4}{2}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{8}{2},\\frac{0}{2}) \\\\  & =(-4,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e9df1ae-8176-555b-987d-94773c27d435" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Distance Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f43b441b-b7a8-5128-ab59-60185fc919bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267175} {:answer/id #uuid "f2279866-4acd-5475-8a6d-bd65e65ecba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267176} {:answer/id #uuid "5d567fd6-85b7-50ab-bb22-3223e809e09a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267177} {:answer/id #uuid "eda0f673-7b3d-530b-8c8e-5f22f4047cfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267178} {:answer/id #uuid "39dfecd7-2792-5cf9-b447-5b0e6ecec70c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eda0f673-7b3d-530b-8c8e-5f22f4047cfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267178} :answer-field/id #uuid "24893160-99df-570f-86da-247de66767be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267174}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47fb0866-8c5c-5b29-b9d5-6b7077659c63" :question/math-academy-id "q-115360" :question/problem "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-3,-4)$ and $(0,-4)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Find the radius of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3-0)^{2}+(-4-(-4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52384502-66c5-5089-b38f-d46b94877430" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7ff976b-cb6a-5fd7-9627-4fbed1c64a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,3)$ and the radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267182} {:answer/id #uuid "0b992e18-356c-5845-aa6b-2e100e2ef380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,4)$ and the radius is $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267183} {:answer/id #uuid "93793513-b2d5-59e6-aa3d-17479745b092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,4)$ and the radius is $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267184} {:answer/id #uuid "20fdaec5-9333-5757-9e87-c84ae49ecb37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,3)$ and the radius is $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267185} {:answer/id #uuid "14441f1d-03e5-5b3a-b7c1-9daf4540e8d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,3)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14441f1d-03e5-5b3a-b7c1-9daf4540e8d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,3)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267186} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cf9a08a-c5ba-5948-a222-2d7b38169f05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267181}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a02e3599-0d24-591c-985f-c45e9f652ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-115364" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956659/assets/3af3101fd7a103e8382755177ca1ebab9bc1cdf48aebd34af8ac7cc92991387c.png)\n\nGiven that the points $(-1,2)$ and $(1,4)$ lie on a diameter of a circle, what are the center and radius of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-1+1}{2},\\frac{2+4}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{6}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(0,3)$ and a point on the circle, such as $(-1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-1-0)}^{2}+{(2-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d68c23-6a62-538d-adf1-3a20a474f107" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Midpoint Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34200cda-d48f-51ab-8d15-fd0c2422a3e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267189} {:answer/id #uuid "68f47835-ee74-59f3-904c-98ac2916303f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68f47835-ee74-59f3-904c-98ac2916303f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267190} :answer-field/id #uuid "499eb9c8-127e-597d-9375-4b022b7ba625" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a84cfcfd-d48d-5eb1-803c-0ff225ffa1cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a84cfcfd-d48d-5eb1-803c-0ff225ffa1cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267192} :answer-field/id #uuid "02671327-8643-5ac5-b72b-8c5448bae99b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267191}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f909f884-706c-5d31-a3a9-05dffd57f7a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-263114" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956659/assets/d8674de78fc4c8685eb5e76c6beb30e08717ff74d411c71e4c25b784516e3ee8.png)\n\nFind the coordinates $(h,k)$ of the center of the circle above given that the points $(6,-4)$ and $(2,4)$ lie on a diameter of the circle.\n\n$(h,k)=(${{field-1}}$,${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. Therefore, we can calculate it using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{6+2}{2},\\frac{-4+4}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{2},\\frac{0}{2}) \\\\  & =(4,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e9df1ae-8176-555b-987d-94773c27d435" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Distance Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bab50fa-f609-5d45-a874-88029200b8c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bab50fa-f609-5d45-a874-88029200b8c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267195} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb79c607-4dfa-5dd4-8799-e9b1843726ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267194}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92d71b8d-a6cb-5c28-8e34-cd28a170231b" :question/math-academy-id "q-263123" :question/problem "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-6,-4)$ and $(6,1)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Determine the radius $r$ of the circle.\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6-6)^{2}+(-4-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{13}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e9df1ae-8176-555b-987d-94773c27d435" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Distance Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7ca3d72-eb97-56c8-ae38-8b8fd0c6bc28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7ca3d72-eb97-56c8-ae38-8b8fd0c6bc28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267198} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1131fbc-fb07-5469-b1f1-34075ac0a0d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267197}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7a2172d-47d5-55a4-bfba-9edbee7bffb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-263134" :question/problem "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-3,-4)$ and $(9,8)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Determine the radius $r$ of the circle.\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3-9)^{2}+(-4-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{288} \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{2}=6\\sqrt{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52384502-66c5-5089-b38f-d46b94877430" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1143a57-d9ca-552f-83b6-95f84afd424c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267201} {:answer/id #uuid "49105755-7973-5680-931d-5f7905d988c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49105755-7973-5680-931d-5f7905d988c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267202} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1169bc1-ab00-54fe-a446-da8d032fa47e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267200} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "169f1da7-4d29-5d14-a805-70664f1a35c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "169f1da7-4d29-5d14-a805-70664f1a35c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267204} :answer-field/id #uuid "1761446f-0215-54a0-883e-15b49b3acb33" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9510928c-2dfd-542c-9fb1-2a1aec511d76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9510928c-2dfd-542c-9fb1-2a1aec511d76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267206} :answer-field/id #uuid "63a94b8e-4d5b-595a-b7f1-ef92ba3462e7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267205}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c222bb01-f724-5bcc-bdd1-eb24868f74e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-263144" :question/problem "The segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is the diameter of a circle where the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-7,2)$ and $(5,-6)$, respectively. Find the coordinates of the center and the radius of the circle.\n\nThe circle is centered at  $(${{field-1}}$,${{field-2}}$)$ and its radius is{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-7+5}{2},\\frac{2+(-6)}{2}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{2},-\\frac{4}{2}) \\\\  & =(-1,-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(-1,-2)$ and a point on the circle, such as $(5,-6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-1-5)}^{2}+{(-2-(-6))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,-2),$ and its radius is $2\\sqrt{13}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52384502-66c5-5089-b38f-d46b94877430" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69f421ec-92cb-53d4-b70e-b920d4c593c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69f421ec-92cb-53d4-b70e-b920d4c593c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267209} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9d85eaa-a178-5828-821a-40be70e773ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c2bb1f-96d2-5909-8249-267b3577d352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c2bb1f-96d2-5909-8249-267b3577d352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267211} :answer-field/id #uuid "0855d6f4-4b04-536d-b3df-e1d329d80fc3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267210} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94cbaf7e-ce1e-5614-8ee8-2b2ed906d005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94cbaf7e-ce1e-5614-8ee8-2b2ed906d005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267213} :answer-field/id #uuid "d33ed024-a643-542a-a041-8b9d487f51f7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267212}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "606e5137-bc60-51a7-b5d5-2fd0110d4c66" :question/math-academy-id "q-263155" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956659/assets/752774e8849a8dfbb2badb1124b4be72f585751d7051eddb57d64c471990ec08.png)\n\nGiven that the points $(4,5)$ and $(2,-3)$ lie on a diameter of a circle, what are the center and radius of the circle?\n\nThe circle is centered at  $(${{field-1}}$,${{field-2}}$)$ and its radius is{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4+2}{2},\\frac{5+(-3)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{6}{2},\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  & =(3,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(3,1)$ and a point on the circle, such as $(4,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(3-4)}^{2}+{(1-5)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(3,1),$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{17}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52384502-66c5-5089-b38f-d46b94877430" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f3c5222-f7e1-5752-b1b9-50fef71b99ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f3c5222-f7e1-5752-b1b9-50fef71b99ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267216} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bea43a8-4548-5066-afb1-a18f7f399941" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267215} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8caaff0e-df74-5887-b57c-3eb9c644b3fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8caaff0e-df74-5887-b57c-3eb9c644b3fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267218} :answer-field/id #uuid "77efc2e1-01eb-5e87-a83f-