),$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{65}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e9df1ae-8176-555b-987d-94773c27d435" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Distance Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d9555ed-f64a-53ac-b49f-0948ac794c53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267223} {:answer/id #uuid "deee73bd-b774-5898-8e04-cd233a863793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267224} {:answer/id #uuid "b9be389d-8b3d-5e09-abf9-64de777f6758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267225} {:answer/id #uuid "d25203c6-c765-5ed6-98f4-156d71e41431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267226} {:answer/id #uuid "08a0f6f0-6cd7-51af-90cf-dc036c3508c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08a0f6f0-6cd7-51af-90cf-dc036c3508c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267227} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b8d05cf-7302-5e3e-bb76-828dfe177d1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267222}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec3e941d-cab9-5c3e-9dc1-cc58481fa257" :question/math-academy-id "q-45750" :question/problem "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(0,-7)$ and $(6,1)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Find the radius of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(0-6)}^{2}+{(-7-1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{10}{2}=5\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e9df1ae-8176-555b-987d-94773c27d435" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Distance Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aad6cba0-6222-5325-8f66-4aaddd08db46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267230} {:answer/id #uuid "1bebaea8-77f7-5078-9888-d887fcd38b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267231} {:answer/id #uuid "405d0b65-c4f4-5fb2-9c41-457cd06d7699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267232} {:answer/id #uuid "4c1a6592-9ad1-557b-a713-2d367d0649a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267233} {:answer/id #uuid "85727010-5eec-512c-ada2-e93da59d4867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bebaea8-77f7-5078-9888-d887fcd38b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267231} :answer-field/id #uuid "058c2d79-6572-5f67-aaad-b6d6ea9eb9eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267229}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0e8bc62-0962-5927-ab0b-d84fffd7afcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-45759" :question/problem "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(0,-3)$ and $(4,-5)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Find the radius of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(4-0)}^{2}+(-5-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{(-2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d68c23-6a62-538d-adf1-3a20a474f107" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Midpoint Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a1f3ba8-1f99-5b1f-8079-575f369ff713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267237} {:answer/id #uuid "db5e1588-4b47-5592-9b01-cb30b6866677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267238} {:answer/id #uuid "9e681819-50a4-528e-971e-595be9ed825c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267239} {:answer/id #uuid "7febbc63-e5d3-5b87-a5f7-4b59f3946789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267240} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ca612f-100e-5838-940e-8c5f23ba07a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7febbc63-e5d3-5b87-a5f7-4b59f3946789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267240} :answer-field/id #uuid "34d5a433-c836-5406-aa43-8027cea2baf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267236}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "046a34f6-2239-5695-b83a-4a2ab759acc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-45760" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956659/assets/84b85eabb9e2819cf87d3566cabd1d8a7d6c45285c2628f2c916a68b38e6d420.png)\n\nFind the coordinates $(h,k)$ of the center of the circle above given that the points $(-2,6)$ and $(10,-10)$ lie on a diameter of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. Therefore, we can calculate it using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-2+10}{2},\\frac{6-10}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{2},-\\frac{4}{2}) \\\\  & =(4,-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52384502-66c5-5089-b38f-d46b94877430" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Radius of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ce10c5-83f7-5561-819c-a7999739cc4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(b,3b)$ and the radius is $3|b|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267244} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9225ba-b540-5fd4-a46f-aabc47564bc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(b,2b)$ and the radius is $4b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267245} {:answer/id #uuid "70c6ffab-f545-56db-b6a5-e8ce1293b342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,2b)$ and the radius is $5b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267246} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb6cdc8-cb29-5dfe-866e-ed6770490d45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,b)$ and the radius is $3b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267247} {:answer/id #uuid "03ed36a9-8ced-52d7-9635-dfd92ba6643f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(b,b)$ and the radius is $5|b|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70c6ffab-f545-56db-b6a5-e8ce1293b342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,2b)$ and the radius is $5b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267246} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c541cd1-b41b-5265-bd1f-577fa0198aeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267243}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1ed57943-8c13-5d28-8950-36097beaedf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-54052" :question/problem "The segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is the diameter of a circle where the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(3b,6b)$ and $(-3b,-2b)$, respectively, with $b>0.$ Find the coordinates of the center and the radius of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. So, we can calculate the coordinates of the center using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{3b+(-3b)}{2},\\frac{6b+(-2b)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{4b}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,2b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius can be found by calculating the distance between the center $(0,2b)$ and a point on the circle, such as $A(3b,6b):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0-3b)^{2}+(2b-6b)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3b)^{2}+(-4b)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{b}^{2}+16{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{b}^{2}} \\\\  & =5|b|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $b>0,$ we have that \n\n$$\nr=5|b|=5b.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center of the circle is at $(0,2b)$ and the radius is $5b.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267249 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d68c23-6a62-538d-adf1-3a20a474f107" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Midpoint Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6217945-0ae6-5c87-93e1-f99dd7406527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267251} {:answer/id #uuid "6a704a1d-b240-50ca-a42b-a6a921106b31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267252} {:answer/id #uuid "ed03f4d2-cbac-5adf-948c-e228da7b3ea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267253} {:answer/id #uuid "f8569e6d-1e5c-5557-9f11-f681409d766f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267254} {:answer/id #uuid "74a73a74-0740-57f6-a09b-eb5e894e0327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8569e6d-1e5c-5557-9f11-f681409d766f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267254} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ec76ef-e790-5670-ae76-65158315d3e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267250}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca442907-6c8f-54f4-a844-59603b7072ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-70868" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956659/assets/537e4113338eebfe5ee318d35fb43ea2952bdc48b4f02f68b5ef097626b5d2c0.png)\n\nFind the coordinates $(h,k)$ of the center of the circle above given that the points $(0,2)$ and $(8,4)$ lie on a diameter of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. Therefore, we can calculate it using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(h,k) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0+8}{2},\\frac{2+4}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{2},\\frac{6}{2}) \\\\  & =(4,3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d68c23-6a62-538d-adf1-3a20a474f107" :knowledge-point/title "Determining t